    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "rpc: unify the TX decode failure error message",
    "user": {
      "login": "MrHodlX",
      "id": 289396684,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOET_XzA",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289396684?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/MrHodlX",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MrHodlX/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Eight RPCs had the same \"TX decode failed\" advice pasted in, and it was drifting\r\nbetween wordings. This puts the advice in one inline constexpr string_view constant\r\n(TX_DECODE_ERROR_HINT) in rpc/util.h and uses it from sendrawtransaction,\r\ntestmempoolaccept, submitpackage, generateblock, combinerawtransaction,\r\nsignrawtransactionwithkey, signrawtransactionwithwallet, and importprunedfunds.\r\n\r\nThe hint itself stays (#19836 added it on purpose). The message now names serialization\r\nand hex encoding separately instead of only blaming empty inputs, since the same\r\nerror also fires on invalid hex and truncated or padded serialization.\r\n\r\nArray RPCs now report the failing index instead of echoing the raw hex back (which\r\ncould be huge), matching what combinerawtransaction already did. simulaterawtransaction\r\nkeeps its own generic \"hex string decoding failure\" message.\r\n\r\nRequired test updates ride with the code; the second commit adds malformed-payload\r\ncoverage in rpc_rawtransaction.\r\n",
